          "distinct": true,
          "id": "3a6749883e985cf869ed0b2e71b0b4a9e183cf06",
          "message": "refactor: convert the signature of a query plan `CheckImpl` to return a single path instead of a PathSeq (#2993)\n\n<!--\nIf your PR is not ready to be reviewed or merged, please submit it as a\n\"draft\".\n-->\n\n## Description\n\nThis is a performance benefit and retroactive clarification of the\ninterface. Before, the returned PathSeq contained only the potential\npaths ending with the resource/subject pair being checked or an empty\nsequence.\n\nHowever, even for an empty sequence, we still had to build and iterate\nan iterator. Now, combined with the switch to `*Path` checks are cheaper\nand use less memory, as well as being more clear (No path, none exists.\nIf there's an attached caveat, then it's conditional, as per other\npaths)\n\n## Testing\n\n<!--\nHow did you test this and how can reviewers test this?\n-->\n\n## References\n\n<!--\nGitHub Issue, Discord or Slack threads, etc.\n-->",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-01T10:43:19-07:00",
