          "distinct": true,
          "id": "826838068192930cea0554b19fac56ae188bad69",
          "message": "fix: wildcards in query planner (#3039)\n\n## Description\n\nNoticing the error `\"ERROR: index \\\"pk_relation_tuple\\\" cannot be used\nfor this query (SQLSTATE 42809)\"` led to finding an inconsistency in\narguments being sent from the query planner's datastore abstraction when\nrequesting relations that matched wildcards.\n\nThis PR cleans up the handling of wildcards within query planner by\nmaking them an expected part of the Path returns. This means `Arrow`s\nneed to handle wildcards properly as well, and so on up the chain,\nmatching behavior from previous implementations.\n\nIt also calls the right shape (or no shape) for AllSubjectsForResources\ndepending on the call.\n\n## Testing\n\nLocal testing and integration testing against CRDB\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Maria Ines Parnisari <maria.ines.parnisari@authzed.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-17T21:19:29Z",
