          "distinct": true,
          "id": "8a01e6974dd631a5fe1fe39dd09b4bb7a4752786",
          "message": "chore: use otter as the primary cache implementation and get rid of alternative implementations (#3112)\n\n## Description\nWe've had three alternative implementations for a while now, with\n`ristretto` being the one that is available by default, with two other\nimplementations behind flags. We've load tested this internally and it\nappears that all three of the implementations are interchangeable from a\nperformance perspective. `otter` is the most modern of the three and it\nsupports generics, which means that we don't have to muck around with\ncalculating our own keys.\n\nThis PR makes otter the primary cache, removes the other\nimplementations, and simplifies where possible.\n\n## Changes\nWill annotate.\n\n## Testing\nReview. See that benchmarks are the same.",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-14T22:04:09Z",
