          "distinct": true,
          "id": "11a0b91b597e3deef8c458f67f18ada491e1e450",
          "message": "feat: introduce a hand-written serialize/deserialize for iterators (#3122)\n\n## Description\n\nFor both DispatchQueryPlan, as well as cursoring DispatchQueryPlan, we\nneed some way to serde the iterator tree, and we'd like to do it quickly\n(ie, not with deep protos). This is pretty fast, as the benchmarks\nattest; Serialize takes about 1µs if it's small, maybe 12µs if it's\nparticularly large. And about double that time on the Deserialize\n(2/24).\n\nThe follow up to this PR is twofold:\n- Finish cursors, adding a flag to save intermediate state\n- Unblock using it in DispatchQueryPlan\n  - To send fewer dispatches\n- To send exact trees for execution (which, incidentally, might be as\nfast/faster than reconstructing the plan as we do today)\n\n\n## Testing\n\nTesting and benchmarks in the change",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-20T15:46:11-07:00",
          "tree_id": "42da88fd573dd31b88964b4f7a6c62cf815e5784",
