          "distinct": true,
          "id": "49ef12ea31be753e6096b17f2162dbcb1cdb9d45",
          "message": "fix(schemacache): supervisor recovers from transient watch errors (#3134)\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaces the one-shot watch goroutine in the watching schema cache\n(`--enable-experimental-watchable-schema-cache`) with a supervisor that\nclassifies errors via a deny-list and applies bounded exponential\nbackoff. The cache now recovers from transient watch errors without a\nprocess restart.\n\nAlthough the original reproduction is staged with a Postgres-style\nerror, the previous permanent-fallback path was datastore-agnostic and\nreachable from every backend.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `internal/datastore/proxy/schemacaching/watchingcache.go`, the\nschema-watch goroutine only retried when the error was a\n`datastore.WatchRetryableError`. Any other error type — including\n`WatchDisconnectedError`, bare unwrapped errors from datastore\n`default:` branches, and unknown error types — called\n`setFallbackMode()` and `return`ed. There was no supervisor and no\nrecovery path. The retry counter was also a lifetime cap\n(`maximumRetryCount = 10`), never reset on success, so a long-running\npod that accumulated 11 transient blips would also fall back\npermanently.\n\n## Fix\n\nA new supervisor goroutine drives the watch:\n\n- **Deny-list classification (`isTerminalWatchError`).** Only\n`WatchCanceledError`, `WatchDisabledError`, and direct context\ncancellation are terminal. Everything else — `WatchRetryableError`,\n`WatchDisconnectedError`, bare unwrapped errors, unknown types, watch\nchannel closing without error — is recoverable. Should be fine because\nWatch API is read-only operations.\n- **Exponential backoff** via `github.com/cenkalti/backoff/v5`\n(`InitialInterval=100ms`, `Multiplier=2.0`, `RandomizationFactor=0.5`,\n`MaxInterval=30s`). `ExponentialBackOff` is used directly;\n`backoff.Retry()` is intentionally avoided because its default 15-minute\n`MaxElapsedTime` would silently stop the supervisor.\n- **Reset on success.** `bo.Reset()` fires when a cycle consumes any\nevent (change or checkpoint), so individual transient blips don't\naccumulate toward a cap.\n- **Cycle extraction (`runWatchOnce`).** The previous restart loop body\nis now a self-contained method returning `(error, consumedEvent bool)`.\nThe supervisor calls it in a loop, refreshing `HEAD` per cycle so long\noutages don't expire the revision.\n- **`startSync` is now async.** The previous `wg.Wait()` barrier is gone\n— only the test suite observed it. Existing tests adopt\n`require.Eventually(!inFallbackMode, ...)`, the same pattern the repro\ntest already used.\n\n## New metrics\n\n- `spicedb_datastore_watching_schema_cache_cycle_restarts_total` —\ncounter, incremented at the start of every cycle after the first. A\ngrowing rate flags a flapping watch.\n- `spicedb_datastore_watching_schema_cache_last_event_timestamp_seconds`\n— gauge, set to the wall-clock timestamp (fractional seconds, Prometheus\n`*_timestamp_seconds` convention) every time an event is consumed.\nDashboards build \"time since last event\" as `time() - <metric>`.\n\n## Tests\n\nIn `internal/datastore/proxy/schemacaching/watchingcache_test.go`:\n\n- `TestIsTerminalWatchError` — table test for the classification helper.\n- `TestSleepHelper`, `TestNewSupervisorBackoff` — unit coverage for the\nnew helpers.\n- `TestWatchingCacheRecoversFromTransientError` — repro flipped: after a\ntransient error, the cache exits fallback when the next valid event\narrives.\n- `TestWatchingCacheRecoversAcrossMultipleErrors` — 5 error→event cycles\ncomplete in under 2 s, proving `bo.Reset()` works (without it the 5th\niteration alone would be ~1.6 s and total would exceed 3 s).\n- `TestWatchingCacheTerminatesOnContextCancellation`,\n`TestWatchingCacheTerminatesOnWatchDisabled` — confirm the supervisor\nexits cleanly on terminal cases (no goroutine leaks via `goleak`, no\nfurther `cycle_restarts_total` advancement).\n- `TestWatchingCacheIncrementsCycleRestartsOnRecovery`,\n`TestWatchingCacheUpdatesLastEventTimestamp` — metric coverage.\n\nThe previous `TestPostgresTransientErrorsAreResettable` is removed: the\nsupervisor's correctness no longer depends on per-datastore\n`IsResettableError` matching. Widening that classifier is an optional\nfollow-up (log hygiene only).\n\n## Behavior summary\n\n| Error class | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bare unwrapped datastore error | Permanent fallback | Backed-off\nretry; cache recovers |\n| `WatchRetryableError` | Retry up to 10 lifetime, then permanent\nfallback | Backed-off retry; cache recovers |\n| `WatchDisconnectedError` | Permanent fallback | Backed-off retry;\ncache recovers |\n| `WatchCanceledError` | Permanent fallback | Permanent fallback\n(shutdown — intended) |\n| `WatchDisabledError` | Permanent fallback | Permanent fallback\n(datastore unsupported — intended) |",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-25T13:21:11-07:00",
