          "distinct": true,
          "id": "95522074bcc63066c9fb618718cbe4598258ed66",
          "message": "chore: rework handles for gRPC tests (#3147)\n\n## Description\nThis started out as an adventure to get rid of deprecation warnings\naround `WithBlock`, as these [are\ndiscouraged](https://github.com/grpc/grpc-go/blob/master/Documentation/anti-patterns.md)\nby the gRPC docs. It turned into more of a rabbit hole when I followed\nthe call stack up and found interfaces that didn't make sense to me.\n\nThe main idea is to split out the testing functions from the\n`RunnableServer` interface and change how the buffcon Listeners are\nstood up and passed around.\n\nIt also changes how clients are created, which potentially introduces an\nissue around a race between servers and clients, but a client\nconfiguration that makes the client `waitForReady` should avoid this.\n\n## Changes\nWill annotate.\n\n## Testing\nReview. See that tests pass.",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-09T01:30:00Z",
          "tree_id": "ea0001aa9900a74c7ecae688456d0b665ea43945",
