          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2ff0a385b18609a1194e14aabec0624bf5ef19d8",
          "message": "fix(datastore): prevent optimized revision singleflight from wedging the server (#3142)\n\n* fix(datastore): prevent optimized revision singleflight from wedging the server\n\nThe optimized revision computation runs under singleflight, which replaces\nthe caller's context with one whose deadline has been stripped\n(context.WithoutCancel) and is only cancelled once every awaiting caller\nhas gone away. As a result, a hung datastore call on this path (e.g. a\nhalf-open TCP connection silently dropped by a load balancer) could block\nthe in-flight computation indefinitely. Because every API request needs an\noptimized revision and they all de-duplicate onto that single call, one\ndead connection could wedge the entire server.\n\nThis makes three complementary changes:\n\n- Bound the shared, singleflighted computation with a low timeout so a\n  wedged call cannot pin the latency of every waiting caller and inflate\n  the system-wide P99. The healthy computation takes single-digit ms, so\n  the bound is generous for the happy path.\n\n- On a failed shared attempt, retry the computation directly (outside of\n  singleflight) on the caller's own context, bounded by the caller's\n  deadline (with a fallback for deadline-less callers). This keeps the\n  aggressive shared bound from turning a transient wedge into a failed\n  request; the retry is naturally throttled by the connection pool size.\n\n- Bound the pgxpool acquire-time liveness ping via PingTimeout, exposed as\n  a configurable connection-pool setting (default 5s) for both Postgres and\n  CockroachDB read and write pools, so a half-open connection cannot hang\n  acquisition. This is the only liveness ping pgxpool performs and it was\n  previously unbounded.\n\n* fix(datastore): address review feedback\n\n- Hide the connection ping-timeout flags (keep the 5s default) until load\n  testing settles a good default\n- Emit a span event on the optimized-revision direct-retry path so the\n  fallback is visible in traces, not just logs\n- Return the caller's context error when its context is already done\n- Rename optimizedRevisionTimeout -> optimizedRevisionSharedTimeout for clarity\n- Document the fix in CHANGELOG (singleflight wedge fix applies to all\n  datastores; connection ping-timeout to Postgres and CockroachDB)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Maria Ines Parnisari <maria.ines.parnisari@authzed.com>",
